        <ArticleTitle>PRISMA 2020 compliance in randomized controlled trials: a meta-epidemiological study</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The PRISMA 2020 statement provides updated guidance for reporting systematic reviews. This meta-epidemiological study assessed compliance with PRISMA 2020 among 500 systematic reviews published in high-impact medical journals from 2021 to 2023. Overall compliance was 58.4% (95% CI: 54.1–62.7). Items most frequently omitted were search strategy documentation (item 7), risk of bias assessment (item 12), and certainty of evidence (item 15). Journals requiring PRISMA checklists at submission showed significantly higher compliance scores (p &lt; 0.001). These findings highlight the need for stronger editorial policies and author education regarding PRISMA 2020 requirements.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
