        <ArticleTitle>Automation tools for systematic review screening: a comparative evaluation of Rayyan, Covidence, and Abstrackr</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Systematic review software tools can streamline the screening process. We conducted a head-to-head comparison of Rayyan, Covidence, and Abstrackr across 12 systematic review teams. Outcome measures included time-to-completion, inter-rater agreement (Cohen's kappa), user satisfaction, and error rates. Rayyan showed the highest user satisfaction score (8.4/10) and lowest learning curve. Covidence performed best for inter-rater agreement (kappa = 0.82). Abstrackr's machine learning assistance reduced screening time by 41% compared to manual-only approaches. All three tools were significantly faster than manual screening using spreadsheets (p &lt; 0.05). Selection of tool should be guided by team size, budget constraints, and desired ML assistance level.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
