        <ArticleTitle>Bibliometric analysis of systematic review methodology research: trends from 2000 to 2021</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>We conducted a bibliometric analysis of 4,821 articles on systematic review methodology published between 2000 and 2021. Publication output grew 8.3-fold over the period. The top productive countries were the USA (28.4%), UK (16.1%), and Australia (11.3%). Co-authorship network analysis identified three major research clusters: statistical methods, reporting guidelines, and technology-assisted reviews. Keyword co-occurrence analysis revealed increasing interest in network meta-analysis, living systematic reviews, and artificial intelligence applications. The Cochrane Collaboration and the EQUATOR Network were the most influential organizations. Our findings map the intellectual structure of systematic review methodology research and identify emerging trends for future investigation.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
